# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# terraform/.gitignore — Files Terraform Should Never Commit
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# STATE FILES — NEVER commit to Git
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# terraform.tfstate and *.tfstate.backup contain:
#   - AWS resource IDs (security groups, subnet IDs, etc.)
#   - Sensitive outputs marked as 'sensitive' in outputs.tf
#   - Even non-sensitive values that reveal infrastructure topology
# With remote S3 backend, local state files are not created.
# But if someone runs `terraform init` before setting up S3, local state appears.
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.backup

# State lock files (created during apply, should not be committed)
.terraform.lock.hcl.backup

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# TERRAFORM DIRECTORY — Generated files, not source code
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# .terraform/ contains downloaded provider binaries and module source code.
# These are large (100MB+) and auto-downloaded by `terraform init`.
# Committing them would bloat the repo and cause OS-specific binary issues.
.terraform/

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# VARIABLE FILES — May contain sensitive values
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# terraform.tfvars and *.tfvars files may contain secrets passed as variables.
# Example: MONGO_URI, AWS account IDs, private keys.
# Commit terraform.tfvars.example instead (with placeholder values).
*.tfvars
*.tfvars.json
!*.tfvars.example

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# CRASH LOGS
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
crash.log
crash.*.log

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# GENERATED KUBECONFIG
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# If kubeconfig is generated by Terraform local_file resource:
kubeconfig*
